Aim:-
Demonstrate various data types and operators in python

Algorithm:-
1. Start
2. Input two integers a and b from the user.
3. Compute LHS and RHS of the identity (a + b)² = a² + 2ab + b² and compare them.
4. Compute LHS and RHS of the identity (a − b)² = a² − 2ab + b² and compare them.
5. Compute LHS and RHS of the identity (a + b)(a − b) = a² − b² and compare them.
6. Compute LHS and RHS of the identity a³ + b³ = (a + b)(a² − ab + b²) and compare them.
7. Verify bitwise identities using operators |, &, ^.
8. Compare each LHS and RHS and print whether they are equal.
9. Repeat the comparison for all given expressions.
10.Stop.

code:-
a = int(input("Enter a value: "))
b = int(input("Enter b value: "))


lhs = (a + b) * (a + b)
rhs = (a * a) + (2 * a * b) + (b * b)
print("The eq are:", lhs == rhs)

lhs = (a - b) * (a - b)
rhs = (a * a) - (2 * a * b) + (b * b)
print("The eq are:", lhs == rhs)

lhs = (a + b) * (a + b)
rhs = 2 * ((a * a) - (b * b))
print("The eq are:", lhs == rhs)

lhs = (a + b) * (a - b)
rhs = (a * a) - (b * b)
print("The eq are:", lhs == rhs)

lhs = (a * a * a) + (b * b * b)
rhs = (a + b) * ((a * a) - (a * b) + (b * b))
print("The eq are:", lhs == rhs)


lhs = a | b
rhs = (a ^ b) + (a & b)
print("The eq are:", lhs == rhs)

lhs = a ^ (a & b)
rhs = (a | b) ^ b
print("The eq are:", lhs == rhs)

lhs = b ^ (a & b)
rhs = (a | b) ^ a
print("The eq are:", lhs == rhs)

lhs = (a & b) ^ (a | b)
rhs = a ^ b
print("The eq are:", lhs == rhs)


lhs = a + b
rhs = (a | b) + (a & b)
print("The eq are:", lhs == rhs)

lhs = a + b
rhs = (a ^ b) + 2 * (a & b)
print("The eq are:", lhs == rhs)


lhs = a - b
rhs = (a ^ (a & b)) - ((a | b) ^ a)
print("The eq are:", lhs == rhs)

lhs = a - b
rhs = ((a|b)^b) - ((a|b)^a)
print("The eq are:", lhs == rhs)

lhs = a - b
rhs = (a ^ (a & b)) - (b^(a&b))
print("The eq are:", lhs == rhs)

lhs = a - b
rhs = ((a | b) ^ b) - (b ^ (a & b))
print("The eq are:", lhs == rhs)

